					<![CDATA[
						 <div style="text-align: right;"></div> <p><tt>&gt; YOU HAVE RECEIVED FILE-SCP-5914 - FROM SITE-19</tt></p> <p><tt>&gt; ACCESS FILE: SCP-5914</tt></p> <p><tt>&gt; ACCESSING FILE: SCP-5914&#8230;</tt></p> <p><tt>&gt; ACCESSING TO DOCUMENTS PRESENT IN THE SCP-5914 SLOT.</tt></p> <p><tt>&gt; ACCESSING-FILE: SCP-5914&#8230;</tt></p> <p><tt>&gt; DISPLAYING FILE&#8230;</tt></p> <div class="note"> <h1><span><span style="font-size:150%;">WARNING</span></span></h1> <h3><span>The following SCP file (SCP-5914) has been classified <strong>TOP SECRET</strong> by order of the O5 Council.</span></h3> <h2><span>UNAUTHORISED PERSONNEL WILL BE TERMINATED UPON ATTEMPTING TO ACCESS FILE SCP-5914.</span></h2> <h3><span>NOTE: FILE UNDER REVIEW.</span></h3> <div style="text-align: right;"></div> <div class="anom-bar-container item-5914 clear-6 esoteric apollyon critical amida {$american}"> <div class="anom-bar"> <div class="top-box"> <div class="top-left-box"><span class="item">Item#:</span> <span class="number">5914</span></div> <div class="top-center-box"> <div class="bar-one"></div> <div class="bar-two"></div> <div class="bar-three"></div> <div class="bar-four"></div> <div class="bar-five"></div> <div class="bar-six"></div> </div> <div class="top-right-box"> <div class="level">Level6</div> <div class="clearance"></div> </div> </div> <div class="bottom-box"> <div class="text-part"> <div class="main-class"> <div class="contain-class"> <div class="class-category">Containment Class:</div> <div class="class-text">esoteric</div> </div> <div class="second-class"> <div class="class-category">Secondary Class:</div> <div class="class-text">apollyon</div> </div> </div> <div class="disrupt-class"> <div class="class-category">Disruption Class:</div> <div class="class-text">critical</div> </div> <div class="risk-class"> <div class="class-category">Risk Class:</div> <div class="class-text">amida</div> </div> </div> <div class="diamond-part"> <div class="danger-diamond"><a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/classification-committee-memo">link to memo</a><br /> <div class="arrows"></div> <div class="octagon"></div> <div class="quadrants"> <div class="top-quad"></div> <div class="right-quad"></div> <div class="left-quad"></div> <div class="bottom-quad"></div> </div> <div class="top-icon"></div> <div class="right-icon"></div> <div class="left-icon"></div> <div class="bottom-icon"></div> </div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <hr /> <p><strong>Special Containment Procedures:</strong> Currently, <span style="text-decoration: line-through;">no containment procedures are made to contained SCP-XXXX has been devised.</span> SCP-5914 is being held in Site-19 but not yet to be successfully managed by the Foundation. Any personnel with suggestions for a way to prevent SCP-5914's anomalous abilities or any information regarding its weaknesses/weak spots should report to the Foundation immediately. Any ideas are welcome, regardless of who suggests them. SCP-5914 must be fully contained <span style="text-decoration: line-through;">and be neutralized</span> at all causes. SCP-5914 is only being held temporarily in Foundation custody.<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-773238-1" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" >1</a></sup> Currently, all of the termination methods are impossible due to their anomalous abilities. The entity currently poses an anomaly that can cause a CK-Class Restructuring and ZK-End-of-Reality Class scenario<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-773238-2" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" >2</a></sup>.</p> <p>Any personnel who encounters SCP-5914 must carefully interact with it and see if they can gain any information from the entity about its proper form, anomalous abilities, personality, recent and daily activities.</p> <p><strong>Description:</strong> SCP-5914 is a soulless and non-corporeal<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-773238-3" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" >3</a></sup>entity that takes the forms of any individuals<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-773238-4" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" >4</a></sup>. While not doing its &quot;job,&quot; the subject would take the form of a dark figure that displays an unknown type of dark matter. It is approximately 171 centimeters (cm), or 5 feet and 7.5 inches, with luminescent red eyes<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-773238-5" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" >5</a></sup>. The entity claims that it exists in a place so-called as &quot;The Barreplex&quot;<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-773238-6" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" >6</a></sup> that existed in an unknown multi-dimensional location shows no signs of hostility, is capable of speech and understands all sorts of human languages. However, it has a very disrespectful/vulgar, and immature attitude.</p> <p>SCP-5914 would gather individuals from a universe or different universes chosen by it into a massive spatial cinematic/theatre room created by itself. The spatial theatre room was designated as SCP-5914-01. While inside SCP-5914-01, the subject would gain full control over everything regardless of whatever it is by just a snap of its finger.<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-773238-7" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" >7</a></sup> It would let those individuals watch other universes with different inhabits, different events; however, sometimes, it would also be from separate timelines/realities<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-773238-8" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" >8</a></sup> of the gathered individuals, as it will also expose the secrets, and information that it wants them to know, regardless of whether if the information and secrets of that universe that the anomaly exposed are strict, top-secret, rated as mature, lead to significant consequences, strictly forbidden/not allowed to know, or the information that they have not learned/heard about their world, or the current situation of other worlds. SCP-5914 will not hesitate but directly spill out all answers, and sometimes give them good advice<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-773238-9" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" >9</a></sup>, however, some individuals have been mocked, joke, and insulted by SCP-5914 to any individual who asked/request some information/explanation that they have yet known about what it shows them.</p> <p>The gathered individuals of the subject are not just from other universes. Some of the collected individuals seem to come from different realities/timelines of those universes. Some are not humans, and SCP-5914 also appears to have control over their situations; some of the gathered individuals claim that they were dead is one of the anomalous abilities of SCP-5914. While inside of SCP-5914-01, there is nothing logical at all because the entity is the rules, SCP-5914 is the rules, and to make sure that none of them have to be worried about what is happening back at their home/world, the entity would freeze the time of the universe; it came up to this point that the Foundation has confirmed that SCP-5914 has absolute power.</p> <p>SCP-5914 can gain a large and full amount of information of any individuals, including objects, by just having a slightly fast leak through without even needing to have a second attempt, which would also explain how the entity can come up with preparations, explanations for them in-case if they attempted to ask, or do so.</p> <p>After the entity has finally finished its job, it will transport the gathered individuals back to their universe, continue observing them or other people interested in it for another period. However, despite being an entity with unique knowledge, SCP-5914 lacks in remembering. SCP-5914 can easily forget a subject that it is talking about with the individuals<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-773238-10" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" >10</a></sup>.</p> <p>SCP-XXXX in some occasions it would usually come and visit different universes/realities/timelines instead of gathering individuals and letting them watch other universes or some secrets that it wants them to know<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-773238-11" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" >11</a></sup>. Any fascinating universes that it finds will make it stay. It will remain invisible and watch the events of that universe, or sometimes it would want to make significant changes of that universe using its anomalous abilities to alter everything of that universe, its timelines, resources/inhabits, reality, event/plot, following the anomaly's unpredictable desires, with no individuals in that universe it visits even able to know, or sense that it has already done it.</p> </div> <div class="note"> <p><strong><span style="text-decoration: underline;">Documented-5914-01: Recover</span></strong></p> <p>SCP-5914 was first discovered on the date of October 12th, 2009, when it was in the middle of gathering a group of peoples into SCP-5914-01; this time, it takes the form of an adult with brown hair and eyes, dressed up in a lab coat and wearing glasses. One of the individuals it has gathered is the SCP Foundation researcher on his way to work. As the researcher has stayed undercover for an extended period and witnessed all, the entity exposed the SCP Foundation's information to all gathered individuals. The researcher has reported back to the Foundation what he has seen, including each compiled individuals' reaction. This soon resulted in the dispatching of MTF Lambda-5; however, the location where he is being held is unknown, and because the satellite of the Foundation could not locate where it is, they have had no choice but to aboard the dispatching, the researcher received a new order of the Foundation, is to gather the names of the individuals that're brought into the room and report it back to the Foundation for preparations of memory-erasing. After the reaction was finished, the researcher reported back to the Site and concluded that the Foundation could successfully wipe out their memories.</p> </div> <div class="note"> <p><strong><span style="text-decoration: underline;">Documented-5914-02: Interview Session with Dr. Liu Log:</span></strong><br /> <strong>Interviewed:</strong> Dr. Liu</p> <p><strong>Interviewer:</strong> SCP-5914</p> <p><strong>Foreword:</strong> On July 11th, 2010, SCP-5914 was in the middle of exploring the universe of the Foundation in the form of a young boy. Due to the curiosity of each SCPs that it seeks in Site-19, it was caught by one of the facility guards while in the middle of traveling but did not try to show any signs of resisting; instead, it just put out a smile and decided to let the Foundation guards arrest it. The following interview is conducted between Dr. Liu and SCP-5914.</p> <hr /> <blockquote> <div style="clear:both; height: 0px; font-size: 1px"></div> <p><strong>&lt;Begin Log&gt;</strong></p> <div style="clear:both; height: 0px; font-size: 1px"></div> <p><strong>Dr.Liu:</strong> Hello there, my name is Dr.Liu, and I am here to do an interview session with you.</p> <div style="clear:both; height: 0px; font-size: 1px"></div> <p><strong>SCP-5914:</strong> Yeah, yeah, hello.</p> <div style="clear:both; height: 0px; font-size: 1px"></div> <p><strong>Dr.Liu:</strong> So, I have a few questions.</p> <div style="clear:both; height: 0px; font-size: 1px"></div> <p><strong>SCP-5914:</strong> Is it to ask me why I have exposed the information that is strictly forbidden not to be exposed to the public under any circumstances?</p> <div style="clear:both; height: 0px; font-size: 1px"></div> <p><strong>Dr. Liu:</strong> <em>(Silence for a moment)</em> How did you-</p> <div style="clear:both; height: 0px; font-size: 1px"></div> <p><strong>SCP-5914:</strong> I would guess your wondering like, why do I know, short answer, I know everything, I know what this place is, what it keeps, and the date it was built, I know who are the Site-Directors, I know who runs the Foundation, in-fact I understand how dangerous these &quot;SCPs&quot; are being kept in, mostly one of my favorites are SCP-173, SCP-682, SCP-999, SCP-096, SCP-049, SCP-035, and SCP-106.</p> <div style="clear:both; height: 0px; font-size: 1px"></div> <p><strong>Dr. Liu:</strong> Mhm, and I guess you would know that your actions would have caused those individuals their own lives if it were not for us coming up with the solution of memory wiping, right?</p> <div style="clear:both; height: 0px; font-size: 1px"></div> <p><strong>SCP-5914:</strong> Yeah, but so, what? You guys thought that I do not know you guys do not care about this world; I know a lot about this place and how many terrible things it holds. You have abused the term &quot;Sacrifices are made for the great or good&quot; too much. I mean, I know it is for humanity, but what is the point when you guys even killed a massive amount of humankind, like that time of SCP-001. You guys are too cold there, not like what you've mentioned, being cold, more like being heartless.</p> <div style="clear:both; height: 0px; font-size: 1px"></div> <p><strong>Dr. Liu:</strong> Well, that-</p> <div style="clear:both; height: 0px; font-size: 1px"></div> <p><strong>SCP-5914:</strong> And do not say it was because of the Foundation, the administrator, or the O5 Council; I know that some of you felt bad for the mortal lives, and some are not; however, regardlessly you guys also seem not to be the type of peoples who keeps promises, I have witnessed you have ignored questions of each SCPs in the Foundation, SCP-4051, makes a perfect example. Say, how was he, by the way?</p> <div style="clear:both; height: 0px; font-size: 1px"></div> <p><strong>Dr. Liu:</strong> Wait, I didn't recall that we have an &quot;SCP-4051.&quot;</p> <div style="clear:both; height: 0px; font-size: 1px"></div> <p><strong>SCP-5914:</strong> It's because this is 2012, not 2013. SCP-4051 will be discovered by you guys in 2013, and I'm telling you, that kid is a very kind-hearted boy, <em>(SCP-5914 speaks in a husky, low, and sinister voice)</em> <strong>but you made him suffer!</strong></p> <div style="clear:both; height: 0px; font-size: 1px"></div> <p><strong>Dr. Liu:</strong> <em>(Silence)</em></p> <div style="clear:both; height: 0px; font-size: 1px"></div> <p><strong>SCP-5914:</strong> <em>(SCP-XXXX's voice changes back normally)</em> I believe that you have no more words to say.</p> <div style="clear:both; height: 0px; font-size: 1px"></div> <p><strong>Dr. Liu:</strong> So, will you-</p> <div style="clear:both; height: 0px; font-size: 1px"></div> <p><strong>SCP-5914:</strong> No, I will not follow any of you back to the Foundation nor collaborate. I do care for others. However, you guys are like in my On and Off list only, not only that, but if I do, I will end up the same as the other; I have witnessed a lot. Furthermore, even if you did succeed in killing me, I will just come back to life; you cannot kill a being you have yet known about.</p> <div style="clear:both; height: 0px; font-size: 1px"></div> <p><strong>Dr. Liu:</strong> I see.</p> <div style="clear:both; height: 0px; font-size: 1px"></div> <p><strong>SCP-5914:</strong> Yeah. At least you did not have to witness the fate of a Site-19 researcher named Dr. Laurence.</p> <div style="clear:both; height: 0px; font-size: 1px"></div> <p><strong>Dr. Liu:</strong> Dr. Laurence? I did not remember that the Foundation has a personal name, Laurence.</p> <div style="clear:both; height: 0px; font-size: 1px"></div> <p><strong>SCP-5914:</strong> Well, its because he is from another reality idiot; well, I have been exploring different universes and realities from the past few years, gotten conducted moreover than <em>(Silence for a moment)</em> I do not know, more than a hundred interviews with different researchers.</p> <div style="clear:both; height: 0px; font-size: 1px"></div> <p><strong>Dr. Liu:</strong> Really?</p> <div style="clear:both; height: 0px; font-size: 1px"></div> <p><strong>SCP-5914:</strong> Yeah, I was thinking of choosing this reality as a central &quot;home&quot; of mines. However, I will not be joining the Foundation, helping them, being collaborative with them. It is my decision; everybody knows that.</p> <div style="clear:both; height: 0px; font-size: 1px"></div> <p><strong>Dr. Liu:</strong> Why our reality? But not other universes and other realities?</p> <div style="clear:both; height: 0px; font-size: 1px"></div> <p><strong>SCP-5914:</strong> Hmph, the other universes and realities are very bored. Yet, other universes always have boring events to me now. Sometimes I would even get disturbed by some peoples in those universes too. Still, in this place, it's fascinating. These &quot;SCPs&quot; just came more and more, with no limits of their populations at all. I love to read their files, especially humanoid/anomalies classified as Keter, Thaumiel, and Apollyon object class SCPs that bring in themselves great forms and &quot;anomalous abilities&quot;.</p> <div style="clear:both; height: 0px; font-size: 1px"></div> <p><strong>Dr. Liu:</strong> I see, however, out of curiosity, why did you reveal all of the forbidden information that would lead to significant consequences towards normal individuals?</p> <div style="clear:both; height: 0px; font-size: 1px"></div> <p><strong>SCP-5914:</strong> Wasn't it obvious? I like watching them react to it. I always wanted to observe each of those individual's reactions. I immensely enjoy seeing them being happy, angry, worried, analyzing that information, coming up with theories, even ways to find weak spots, that is all.</p> <div style="clear:both; height: 0px; font-size: 1px"></div> <p><strong>Dr. Liu:</strong> Okay, so is the so-called cinematic room the only place that you have full power overall?</p> <div style="clear:both; height: 0px; font-size: 1px"></div> <p><strong>SCP-5914:</strong> It is just apart of my specialties, sir. Believe me. I am far beyond the expectations of the Foundation. I can change anything, at any time, any moment, <em>(SCP-5914 speaks in a low, husky, and sinister voice)</em> <strong>of this very own reality</strong>.</p> <div style="clear:both; height: 0px; font-size: 1px"></div> <p><strong>Dr. Liu:</strong> <em>(Silence)</em></p> <div style="clear:both; height: 0px; font-size: 1px"></div> <p><strong>SCP-5914:</strong> <em>(SCP-5914 takes a deep breath as it sighs, and the entity's voice changes back to normal)</em> Hah! sike, pranked you! That was not my original voice; I was faking it. You should see the looks on your face. <em>(SCP-5914 begins to laughs for an extended period and stops)</em> I have no urge against humanity; I would only end the universe of yours when I want to; bye now, our little conversation is over.</p> <div style="clear:both; height: 0px; font-size: 1px"></div> <p><strong>Dr. Liu:</strong> Hold on, I have a final question, do you have any origins?</p> <div style="clear:both; height: 0px; font-size: 1px"></div> <p><strong>SCP-5914:</strong> Yes, that, I can give you a hint, come closer.</p> <div style="clear:both; height: 0px; font-size: 1px"></div> <p><em>(Dr. Liu moves near the entity)</em></p> <div style="clear:both; height: 0px; font-size: 1px"></div> <p><strong>SCP-5914:</strong> I am from the &quot;The Barrelplex&quot;.</p> <div style="clear:both; height: 0px; font-size: 1px"></div> <p><strong>Dr. Liu:</strong>Barrel of what?</p> <div style="clear:both; height: 0px; font-size: 1px"></div> <p><strong>SCP-5914:</strong> No idiot, I am from the &quot;The Barrelplex&quot;.</p> <div style="clear:both; height: 0px; font-size: 1px"></div> <div style="clear:both; height: 0px; font-size: 1px"></div> <p><strong>SCP-5914:</strong> Nah, that is all I can provide, from now. By the way, I jumped to a conclusion very fast; I have decided to turn this place into my main home; after all, I want to witness the fascinating and unknown things of the SCP universe. I love it, anyway. Bye.</p> <div style="clear:both; height: 0px; font-size: 1px"></div> <p><em>(SCP-5914 spontaneously disappears.)</em></p> <div style="clear:both; height: 0px; font-size: 1px"></div> <p><strong>&lt;End Log&gt;</strong></p> </blockquote> </div> <br /> After this, Dr. Liu reported back to the Foundation that SCP-5914 only collaborates/help with the Foundation whenever it wants and described its personality as acting in a vulgar and immature attitude. The origins of SCP-5914 are unknown. What is known is that it came from a place known as &quot;The Barrelplex&quot;. <div class="note"> <p><strong><span style="text-decoration: underline;">Documented-XXXX-03: Update Containment Procedures:</span></strong><br /> On December 12th, 2012, SCP-5914 arrived back at the Foundation. It said that it has decided to turn itself into the Foundation after thinking throughout those two (2) years of exploring this world due to fascination. It told the Foundation of what containment procedures that it wants. However, the Foundation has ordered every person to keep an eye on the entity; every surveillance is installed in every area of its containment chamber.</p> <div class="collapsible-block"> <div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Excerpt-Update&nbsp;Containment&nbsp;Procedures-Log</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none"> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">ACCESS&nbsp;GRANTED</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-content"></div> <div style="border:solid 1px #999999; background:#f2f2c2; padding:5px; margin-bottom: 10px;"> <p><strong>Update Containment Procedures:</strong> SCP-5914 is to be kept at Site-19 inside of an airtight enclosure consists of four adjoining rooms constructed out from alloy steel, 3&#160;m from floor to ceiling, with the following attributes:</p> <ul> <li>* A 24 x 24 x 10 x 10 room is designed to look like a theatre.</li> </ul> <ul> <li>One 5&#160;m x 5&#160;m receiving room with an airlock and seating appropriate for SCP-5914.</li> </ul> <ul> <li>One 20&#160;m x 15&#160;m dining area.</li> </ul> <ul> <li>One 5&#160;m x 5&#160;m sleep area and rest facility, furnished with seating and bedding.</li> </ul> <p>The entity is allowed to wander the facility anytime it wants<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-773238-12" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" >12</a></sup>; food, drinks, and entertaining kinds of stuff are unnecessary because the entity would already provide itself with what it needs.</p> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class="note"> <p><strong><span style="text-decoration: underline;">Documented-5914-04: Event Logs.</span></strong></p> <p>These are all of the records of SCP-5914's daily and recent activities in the Foundation daily. <span style="text-decoration: line-through;">This includes events, such as gathering individuals from different universes for its enjoyment in seeing their reactions about the SCPs<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-773238-13" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" >13</a></sup> interacting with other SCPs of Site-19 and using its powers to make some changes inside its containment cell</span>. Due to not collecting a single piece of information through physical interactions with the entity, they have decided to use the event logs recorded on the surveillance and make some transcripts <span style="text-decoration: line-through;">to find some information on the anomaly</span>.</p> <p>The anomaly, however, ever since being held temporarily in Foundation custody, its daily activity from gathering individuals from other realities/timelines/universes somewhat, became less, as it starts to focus on interacting with other SCPs, and only letting them &quot;reacting&quot;/watching things that they have not yet learn, and would sometimes cause out major ruckus upon the universe it is currently in.</p> <div class="collapsible-block"> <div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Excerpt-Event-Log-01</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none"> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">ACCESS&nbsp;GRANTED</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-content"> <div style="border:solid 1px #999999; background:#f2f2c2; padding:5px; margin-bottom: 10px;"> <p><strong>Event Log-01:</strong></p> <p><strong>Recorded on the date of December 14th, 2012.</strong></p> <p><strong>Description:</strong> SCP-5914 performs its first daily routine and activity. The following log also shows that SCP-5914 has breached into the containment chamber of SCP-053 and proceeded to play some games with it.</p> <hr /> <p><strong>&lt;BEGIN LOG&gt;</strong></p> <p>SCP-5914 wakes up and yawns after its napping; it got off the bed and walked out of its room.</p> <p>As it walks into the bathroom, SCP-5914 started to brush its teeth.</p> <p>SCP-5914 then got dressed by shapeshifting itself into a 20 years old young-adult, fixing its hair, and wearing on clothing that fits its style of changing its yesterday outfit.</p> <p>SCP-5914 walks down into the dining room, creating a hamburger, a ketchup bottle, french fries, and a 247 Expresso energy drink bottle.</p> <p>The entity begins to eat.</p> <p>After finishing its breakfast, SCP-5914 gets out from the table, walks forward, and breaches through its containment cell entrance door.</p> <p>SCP-5914 was shown to be wandering near SCP-053's containment cell in the form of a young-adult as it stops and stands in front of SCP-053's containment cell <em><strong>SCP-5914: Oh, l wondered how is that cute little girl is doing?</strong></em></p> <p>SCP-5914 stands for a while as it walks through the entrance door of SCP-053's containment cell.</p> <p>Inside the containment cell, SCP-053 was shown to be staring at SCP-5914 <em><strong>SCP-053: Are you here to play with me?</strong></em> SCP-5914 smiles <em><strong>SCP-5914: Heh, of course, kiddo</strong></em> SCP-5914 walks forward and sits near SCP-053 as they began to play with each other.</p> <p>While SCP-5914 and SCP-053 were in the middle of playing, one of the Foundation's facilities guards has caught them as the agent knocks on the window of SCP-053's containment chamber.</p> <p>SCP-5914 and 053 look over at the facility guard. <em><strong>Facility Guard: Hey? 5914, get out of 053's containment cell, you are not allowed to-</strong></em> SCP-5914 immediately cut off the agent's words <em><strong>SCP-5914: Screw off fucker, we are in the middle of playing</strong></em>.</p> <p>The facility guard has attempted to call for reinforcements; however, SCP-5914 immediately stares at him with its eyes wide. The facility guard suddenly stands still and did not react as they motionlessly walk away.</p> <p>SCP-053 looks back at SCP-5914 as the little girl sees the &quot;young-adult&quot; smiling brightly <em><strong>SCP-5914: Shall we go back to where we are doing, Abby?</strong></em></p> <p>SCP-053 smiles as she nods. SCP-5914 stands up as it snaps its finger. The room got dark. A bright screen showed right in front of them.</p> <p>SCP-5914 smiles brightly <em><strong>SCP-5914: Anyways, want to react to something?</strong></em> SCP-053 nods as she sat on a chair that appeared out of nowhere. What SCP-5914 showed SCP-053 was a comedy kid television TV show known as &quot;The Amazing World of Gumball&quot;.</p> <p>After watching a few episodes and SCP-5914 giving her explanations of what makes the television shoe worth to watch, SCP-5914 soon stood up as it says goodbye to SCP-053 and walks out of the room without having any signs of being affected at all.</p> <p>Later on, SCP-5914 walks back to its containment room and gathers a group of individuals from other universes. It welcomes and begins to explain to them the current situation.</p> <p><strong>&lt;END LOG&gt;</strong></p> <hr /> <p><strong>Note:</strong> SCP-5914 appears to be immune to the effects of SCP-053, as it was also shown to be very social and forms a good relationship with SCP-053 without showing any signs of homicidal or paranoid before walking back to its containment cell for another day of its gathering and reacting, despite having the attitude of an unprofessional, and immature person, it also seems to show out some signs of kindness inside of it. The subject also seems to have a very unhealthy diet.</p> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class="collapsible-block"> <div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Excerpt-Event-Log-02</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none"> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">ACCESS&nbsp;GRANTED</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-content"> <div style="border:solid 1px #999999; background:#f2f2c2; padding:5px; margin-bottom: 10px;"> <p><strong>Event Log-02: Conversation with SCP-343</strong></p> <hr /> <p style="text-align: center;"><strong>VIDEO LOG</strong></p> <hr /> <p><strong>DATE:</strong> December 14th, 2012</p> <p><strong>FOREWORD:</strong> The following footage describes SCP-5914 was encountering SCP-343 as it also attempts to make a brief introduction.</p> <hr /> <p><strong>&lt;BEGIN LOG&gt;</strong></p> <p><strong>&lt;00:20:30&gt; -</strong> SCP-5914 was in the middle of staring at SCP-343 as it walked forward and gave out a brief introduction of itself <em><strong>SCP-5914: Hey there, you must be SCP-343 if I am not wrong?</strong></em>.</p> <p><strong>&lt;00:20:31&gt; -</strong> SCP-343 looks at the entity standing right in front of it SCP-5914 <em><strong>SCP-343: Yes, and you must be that entity that the Foundation was mentioning to me, SCP-5914 was it?</strong></em></p> <p><strong>&lt;00:20:32&gt; -</strong> SCP-5914 looks at SCP-343 <em><strong>SCP-5914: Yes, I cannot argue with that.</strong></em> SCP-5914 smiles as it raises out two of its hands and looks away in a funny attitude.</p> <p><strong>&lt;00:20:33&gt; -</strong> SCP-343 chuckles but stops in a few seconds; after a while of staring at SCP-5914, it begins to ask <em>SCP-343: What exactly are you wanting to tell me?</em> SCP-343 now sees that SCP-5914 is standing in a motionless/lifeless way without responding.</p> <p><strong>&lt;00:20:34&gt; -</strong> SCP-343 looks at it in confused <em>SCP-343: Um, are you alright?</em> SCP-5914 still did not respond; the entity still looks direct at SCP-343 in a motionless way; after a moment of staring at SCP-343, it snaps.</p> <p><strong>&lt;00:20:34&gt; -</strong> <em><strong>SCP-5914: Gah! Oh, shit, sorry about that, I was thinking of something different; anyway, what were we talking about again?</strong></em> SCP-343 looks at SCP-5914 <em>SCP-343: Uh, you came here and talk to me, so may I help you?</em></p> <p><strong>&lt;00:20:35&gt; -</strong> <em><strong>SCP-5914: What, I did?</strong></em> SCP-343 looks at it with eyes widen, SCP-5914 stares at SCP-343 and thinks for a moment as it also realized it <em><strong>SCP-5914: Oh yes, I just only came here to give you a brief introduction of mines; I am sorry if I am bothering you</strong></em> SCP-5914 smiles as it turns around and walks away.</p> <p><strong>&lt;00:20:36&gt; -</strong> <em><strong>SCP-343: Hold it right there.</strong></em> SCP-XXXX stops walking, SCP-343 walks forward at the entity <em><strong>SCP-343: This sense, though what I am sensing now, I would say you do not come from around here at all, you know what I mean, right?</strong></em> SCP-5914 turns around and stares at SCP-343 with its eyes narrowed <em><strong>SCP-5914: How do you know?&quot;</strong></em> SCP-343 looks at the entity <em><strong>SCP-343: Wasn't it obvious? I sense a very overwhelming power inside of you. It is very beyond the regular expectation of anything that I have ever seen, so you do not have anything to hide at all</strong></em> SCP-5914 face suddenly changes into serious as it walks forward and grabs the hand of SCP-343.</p> <p><strong>&lt;00:20:36&gt; -</strong> <em><strong>SCP-5914: Then perhaps I must show you something, but you cannot let anyone know about this, got it?</strong></em> SCP-343 nods as the two SCPs all walked back to SCP-5914's containment cell.</p> <p><strong>&lt;00:20:37&gt; -</strong> Inside of SCP-5914's containment cell, SCP-5914 snaps its finger, and a widescreen opens.</p> <p><strong>&lt;00:20:38&gt; -</strong> <em><strong>SCP-5914: Before we start, I have to do something first.</strong></em> SCP-5914 snaps its finger, and the surveillance of its containment lost signal and did not respond.</p> <p><strong>&lt;!@:!#:@$&gt; -</strong> !@&amp;^$&amp;#^$&amp;#^$&amp;#$#$(%&amp;$(%#(%#&amp;(#$&amp;#($</p> <p><strong>&lt;!@#&amp;:!#@(:@$&gt; -</strong> !@&amp;^$&amp;#^$&amp;##(#$#($*#^$&amp;#$@!#%&amp;%(</p> <p><strong>&lt;02:20:36&gt; -</strong> When the surveillances maintained back naturally, it was found out that it has been recorded for 2 hours now. The surveillance camera is currently being seen as SCP-343 standing up and walks out of SCP-5914's containment cell.</p> <p><strong>&lt;END VIDEO&gt;</strong></p> <hr /> <p><strong>Note:</strong> The interaction between SCP-343 and SCP-5914 was normal; nothing happened at all; however, through those observations, it is highly stated that SCP-5914 can forget a subject doing if it were ever to get distracted by others; however, this may happen sometimes. In short, SCP-5914 is also an airhead. It was discovered that the recording surveillance of the anomaly's containment lasted for 2 hours. It looks like SCP-5914 must-have speed time. A piece of new information was also found. Besides being a disrespectful person, SCP-5914 was shown to have a serious side of it. However, what exactly was it showing to SCP-343? Later on, the Foundation has asked SCP-343 for some information of what SCP-343 has seen in SCP-5914-01 along with SCP-5914. SCP-343 refuses to answer and says that it is the choice of SCP-XXXX to answer or deny since what is revealed to SCP-343 is something that normal humans cannot be allowed to uncover. There is still a question that the Foundation was wondering, what exactly is the &quot;Beyond Bubble&quot;? Moreover, what exists in the &quot;Beyond Bubble&quot;?</p> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class="collapsible-block"> <div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Excerpt-Event-Log-03</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none"> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">ACCESS&nbsp;GRANTED</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-content"> <div style="border:solid 1px #999999; background:#f2f2c2; padding:5px; margin-bottom: 10px;"> <p><strong>Event Log-03:</strong> The Cr███p██ta</p> <p><strong>Recorded on the date of December 16th, 2012.</strong></p> <p><strong>Description:</strong> The following log has shown that SCP-5914 has gathered a group of other individuals from another universe. However, from a different reality of a universe, as it was revealed that the picked subjects are all insane, murderous, and delusional serial killers and hostile entities.</p> <hr /> <p><strong>&lt;BEGIN LOG&gt;</strong></p> <p>This time the anomaly has taken the form of an adult, SCP-5914, who has now shapeshifted its non-physical avatar into a physical avatar with short black hair and brown eyes. It is repeatedly described as a fragile-looking, handsome man with a beautiful face wearing a regular outfit consisting of a black coat with brown fur lining that goes down to its hips and a straight black long-sleeved v-neck pants, and dark brown shoes.</p> <p><em><strong>SCP-5914: *Sighs* It has been such a long time ever since I have not gathered any individuals.</strong></em> SCP-5914 claps its hands as a group of &quot;peoples&quot; were gathered into SCP-5914-01; these groups of individuals all seem to have weird-looking appearances. They were confused, some were angry, some were afraid, and some appears to have recognized one or another who are gathered in the room.</p> <p><em><strong>SCP-5914:</strong> Hello, there ███████, my name is Tony Alan, and sorry if I am bothering you little shits because you all are assholes and-**</em> Without finishing its words, two subjects, one male and female, rushes forward in a breakneck speed and attempted to kill SCP-5914. However, their equipment all disappears into thin air.</p> <p>The female subject seems to have a clock on her right eye <em><strong>Female-01: HUH! WHAT HAPPENED TO OUR WEAPONS?!</strong></em> SCP-5914 has exclaimed with its disrespected and immature attitude <em><strong>SCP-5914: SHUT UP! NOW YAH ALL LISTEN HERE, I'M THE ONE WHOSE INCHARGE IN THIS SHIT, AND NONE OF YAH ARE LIVING UNTIL I SAID SO, GOT IT?!</strong></em></p> <p>A pale humanoid white subject answered back <em><strong>Subject-Humanoid-01: Who are you? What is the meaning of this? And who says that you in charge?</strong></em></p> <p>SCP-5914 laughs as it looks directly at the humanoid subject <em><strong>SCP-5914: Because I said so, now try and be a right audience, because I have already had much stress today having to gathered a group of &quot;universally&quot; hated peoples.</strong></em></p> <p><em><strong>White-Humanoid-Subject-01: //(Silence)</strong></em> <strong>Who are you? What do you want from us?</strong> SCP-5914 looks at the humanoid subject <em><strong>SCP-5914: Reactions, what I want is for you peoples to react, now be nice, and if you attempt to do something stupid like earlier,</strong> //(Speaks in a low, husky, and sinister voice)</em> <strong>I will end your existence from all realities</strong>// SCP-5914's eyes turned red as it stares at them in a very outrageous way. <em><strong>SCP-5914:</strong> //(Voice changes back normally)</em>, <em>(Sighs)</em> <strong>I do not even know why you ███████ cannot understand humanity. I mean, can't you see that your causing despair on them slowly, many peoples have lost their families because of you peoples, I felt bad for them.</strong> White-Humanoid-Subject-01 stood up and spoke out <em><strong>White-Humanoid-Subject-01: It was because they are pathetic and also the caused of turning these previous innocents into-</strong></em></p> <p>SCP-5914 glares at the white humanoid subject as it walks forward, grab the neck of the subject, and crushes it slowly <em><strong>SCP-5914:</strong> //(Speaks in a demonic voice)</em> <strong>I hate peoples like you, killing innocent? I do not know why you choose to kill innocents, but this is so wrong, and when you were about to shout out, &quot;YOU DON'T UNDERSTAND US!&quot; yes, I do not understand you. Gladly I never will, except for little demon and cute little ghost, what was your name again, was it ████ and █████, yeah, that is right.</strong>// SCP-5914 looks at the two short humanoid female subjects who are now trembling in fear after witnessing it; the anomaly sighs as it puts down the white figure.</p> <p><em><strong>SCP-5914: Anyways, I would like you guys to react to something. It is about the SCP-Foundation, yah all are going to be watching, reacting to each SCPs in this god damn room since this is my goddamn night where I would have my god damn free times</strong></em> SCP-5914 looks at the surveillance that was installed inside of its containment cell <em>**SCP-5914: I need some privacies, and by the way Foundation, you already know what the files, so yah motherfuckers don't have to watch this, don't worry they're from different realities of a universe so that it won't be a problem.</em> it snaps its fingers, and the surveillance lost all signals.</p> <p><strong>&lt;END LOG&gt;</strong></p> <hr /> <p>Note: SCP-5914 seems to have a great level of distress and aggression whenever it's near individuals who don't felt sympathy for human beings, as it was shown to have threatened the subject humanoid-01 for calling humanity pathetic, and soon once again caused the surveillances of its containment cell, when one of the personnel were ordered to entered SCP-5914's containment cell, the subject wasn't there, nor with the other gathered subjects of it, assuming that SCP-5914 must've taken them to a different multi-dimensional space where only it, and they are at. And as days pass by, the Foundation could not gather any information about SCP-5914. It also did not let them see what kinds of things it lets the gathered individuals react to. The idea of gathering information through the surveillances was not long later canceled.</p> </div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class="note"> <p><strong><span style="text-decoration: underline;">Documented-5914-06: Incident Log.</span></strong></p> <div class="collapsible-block"> <div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Excerpt-Incident-Log-01</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none"> <div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">ACCESS&nbsp;GRANTED</a></div> <div class="collapsible-block-content"> <p><strong>Documented Incident-5914-01:</strong></p> <p>On 11/12/2013, the Site's power and door control systems begin to malfunction, allowing all SCPs to kill 15% of the personnel of Site-19. It occurred at 9:14 PM when a big broadcast announced that several SCPs had breached containment, forcing the Site to be put under lockdown. However, after 5 minutes have passed by, everything has suddenly gotten back to normal. The power outage went on as all SCPs were transported back to their containment cells. Everything is fully restored to normal. One of the facility guards has caught SCP-5914 and SCP-053 walking through the hallways, as they found out that the cause of the big containment breach event was because of SCP-5914 all along. The anomaly was teaching SCP-053 what happens if the facility has a containment breach before asking the little girl to stop by SCP-5031 to tase some of its food. As Foundation staffs started to gather some information and evidence, they've also found out that the cause of hurting the individuals from the outside world was also because of SCP-5914.</p> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div class="note"> <p><strong><span style="text-decoration: underline;">Documented-5914-05:</span></strong> Interview Session with Researcher Rainwards:</p> <p><strong>Interviewed:</strong>Dr. Rainwards.</p> <p><strong>Interviewer:</strong> SCP-5914</p> <p><strong>Foreword:</strong> Dr. Rainwards was given an ordered to conduct an interview session with SCP-5914 to see whether if he can find any essential information to learn more about its nature.</p> <hr /> <blockquote> <div style="clear:both; height: 0px; font-size: 1px"></div> <p><strong>&lt;Begin Log&gt;</strong></p> <div style="clear:both; height: 0px; font-size: 1px"></div> <p><strong>Dr. Rainwards:</strong> Okay, so, good evening sir; my name is-</p> <div style="clear:both; height: 0px; font-size: 1px"></div> <p><strong>SCP-5914:</strong> Yeah, yeah, no need for the brief introduction; I know what your name is, Dr. Rainwards, was it?</p> <div style="clear:both; height: 0px; font-size: 1px"></div> <p><strong>Dr. Rainwards:</strong> Yes, and I believe that you know the rest.</p> <div style="clear:both; height: 0px; font-size: 1px"></div> <p><em>(SCP-5914 nods while narrowing its eyes with its legs on the table)</em></p> <div style="clear:both; height: 0px; font-size: 1px"></div> <p><strong>Dr. Rainwards:</strong> So, as you can see here, in the previous reports and logs we have had, you seem to be very friendly to all unhostile SCPs. Might you explain to me why?</p> <div style="clear:both; height: 0px; font-size: 1px"></div> <p><strong>SCP-5914:</strong> Sir, for the last time, I am not the wrong person. I mean, what? Are you accusing me of a monster? That is cold as a shithole.</p> <div style="clear:both; height: 0px; font-size: 1px"></div> <p><strong>Dr. Rainwards:</strong> No, we do not accuse you as a monster; however, you seemed to be very pacifist at SCP-053.</p> <div style="clear:both; height: 0px; font-size: 1px"></div> <p><strong>SCP-5914:</strong> Well, yeah, she is a cute little girl, and she does not deserve to have that terrible power, for the first time of meeting up with her; I have already felt bad for her. I wanted to give her a great life. The fuck is happening to the world god?</p> <div style="clear:both; height: 0px; font-size: 1px"></div> <p><strong>Dr. Rainwards:</strong> Mhm, if so, then why didn't you just removed her powers?</p> <div style="clear:both; height: 0px; font-size: 1px"></div> <p><strong>SCP-5914:</strong> Heh, and why should I tell you that? It is my option, whether if I want to or not.</p> <div style="clear:both; height: 0px; font-size: 1px"></div> <p><strong>Dr. Rainwards:</strong> Okay, so in some of the logs, you have stated that your name is Tony Alan. Was that your name?</p> <div style="clear:both; height: 0px; font-size: 1px"></div> <p><strong>SCP-5914:</strong> Then would you believe that is my real name? If that so, then fine, call me so.</p> <div style="clear:both; height: 0px; font-size: 1px"></div> <p><strong>Dr. Rainwards:</strong> <em>(Stayed silent for a moment)</em> O-okay <em>(Coughs)</em> then can you explain to me why did you have to cause such a big containment breach like this?!</p> <div style="clear:both; height: 0px; font-size: 1px"></div> <p><strong>SCP-5914:</strong> It's obvious, SCP-053 needs to learn more about this place, so I've decided to educate her.</p> <div style="clear:both; height: 0px; font-size: 1px"></div> <div style="clear:both; height: 0px; font-size: 1px"></div> <p><strong>Dr. Rainwards:</strong> SCP-5914! Did you know that your actions have caused deaths over the lives of the facility? Over 15% of personnel were dead.</p> <div style="clear:both; height: 0px; font-size: 1px"></div> <p><strong>SCP-5914:</strong> Yes, however, they were all criminals, after all, I mean, after the day when I've first arrived here, I've discovered that the Class D personnel are expendable used to handle extremely hazardous anomalies and are not allowed to come into contact with Class A or Class B personnel. Class D personnel are typically drawn worldwide from the ranks of prison inmates convicted of violent crimes, especially those on death row.</p> <div style="clear:both; height: 0px; font-size: 1px"></div> <p><strong>Dr. Rainwards:</strong> Fine, let's let this slide. Now, can you tell me what exactly is this so-called &quot;The Barrelplex&quot;?</p> <div style="clear:both; height: 0px; font-size: 1px"></div> <p><strong>SCP-5914:</strong> Oh shit, this again, listen, I do not care about what is currently happening in that place; it is none of our shitty business at all; I mean, do not try and annoyed the audience.</p> <div style="clear:both; height: 0px; font-size: 1px"></div> <p><strong>Dr. Rainwards:</strong> Wait? What audience?</p> <div style="clear:both; height: 0px; font-size: 1px"></div> <p><em>(SCP-5914 is shown to be standing on another side of the room staring at the walls as it turns around.)</em></p> <div style="clear:both; height: 0px; font-size: 1px"></div> <p><strong>SCP-5914:</strong> Oh shit, sorry, I was talking to mister walls.</p> <div style="clear:both; height: 0px; font-size: 1px"></div> <p><strong>Dr. Rainwards:</strong> <em>(Silence)</em></p> <div style="clear:both; height: 0px; font-size: 1px"></div> <p><strong>SCP-5914:</strong> What were we talking about again?</p> <div style="clear:both; height: 0px; font-size: 1px"></div> <p><strong>Dr. Rainwards:</strong> <em>(Sighs)</em> Anyways, may I also know the date when you were born?</p> <div style="clear:both; height: 0px; font-size: 1px"></div> <p><strong>SCP-5914:</strong> I do not have one. I was brought to existence as a &quot;mistaken&quot; creation of that &quot;place.&quot;</p> <div style="clear:both; height: 0px; font-size: 1px"></div> <p><strong>Dr. Rainwards:</strong> Place? Do you mean &quot;The Barrelplex&quot;?</p> <div style="clear:both; height: 0px; font-size: 1px"></div> <p><strong>SCP-5914:</strong> Well, yeah&#8230;</p> <div style="clear:both; height: 0px; font-size: 1px"></div> <p><strong>Dr. Rainwards:</strong> May you, please explain to me what exactly is this &quot;The Barrelplex&quot;?</p> <div style="clear:both; height: 0px; font-size: 1px"></div> <p><strong>SCP-5914:</strong> I can't because I do not know what consequences I might bring back to you, and the Foundation, of course. <em>(SCP-5914 slowly looked down and began to muttered)</em> Especially, &quot;them,&quot; &quot;they&quot; are whom I do not want to meet; those bastards think that having their roles as &quot;Gods&quot; means you must be perfect, heh not all &quot;Gods&quot; should be perfect. However, who even said that we are &quot;Gods&quot;? We are not &quot;Gods.&quot;</p> <div style="clear:both; height: 0px; font-size: 1px"></div> <p><strong>Dr. Rainwards:</strong> Who are &quot;they&quot;?</p> <div style="clear:both; height: 0px; font-size: 1px"></div> <p><strong>SCP-5914:</strong> Huh! How did you manage to-?</p> <div style="clear:both; height: 0px; font-size: 1px"></div> <p><strong>Dr. Rainwaeds:</strong> I have a perfect hearing, in short, now please tell me SCP-5914 who are &quot;they?</p> <div style="clear:both; height: 0px; font-size: 1px"></div> <p><em>(Silence from SCP-5914)</em></p> <div style="clear:both; height: 0px; font-size: 1px"></div> <p><strong>SCP-5914:</strong> Oh, you know, just some &quot;familiars&quot; who sees me as a&#8230; &quot;mistaken&quot; to that &quot;place, and existence itself.</p> <div style="clear:both; height: 0px; font-size: 1px"></div> <p><strong>Dr. Rainwards:</strong> Who are these &quot;familiars&quot; of yours. Furthermore, why do you claim that they are not &quot;Gods&quot;?</p> <div style="clear:both; height: 0px; font-size: 1px"></div> <p><strong>SCP-5914:</strong> <em>(SCP-5914 growls aggressively)</em> Just a bunch of delusional entities who are always arrogant and act as if they are superior to anything is, although they are, but not to me, in any case.</p> <div style="clear:both; height: 0px; font-size: 1px"></div> <p><strong>Dr. Rainwards:</strong> Be more specific of who were these &quot;Gods&quot; you talking about?</p> <div style="clear:both; height: 0px; font-size: 1px"></div> <p><strong>SCP-5914:</strong> <em>(Silence for a moment)</em> Um, today we have ice creams in the cafeteria, right? Yes! Let us go and get some.</p> <div style="clear:both; height: 0px; font-size: 1px"></div> <p><em>(SCP-5914 stands up as it proceeded to leave, but Dr. Rainwards stops it)</em></p> <div style="clear:both; height: 0px; font-size: 1px"></div> <p><strong>Dr. Rainwards:</strong> SCP-5914! Can you please tell me who are &quot;they&quot;?</p> <div style="clear:both; height: 0px; font-size: 1px"></div> <p><em>(SCP-5914 stand motionless for a moment as it sighs, walks back, and sits down)</em></p> <div style="clear:both; height: 0px; font-size: 1px"></div> <p><strong>SCP-5914:</strong> This&#8230;is why I always hate peoples who are determined to find answers to everything&#8230; <em>(SCP-5914 stares at Dr. Rainwards.)</em></p> <div style="clear:both; height: 0px; font-size: 1px"></div> <p><strong>Dr. Rainwards:</strong> Well?</p> <div style="clear:both; height: 0px; font-size: 1px"></div> <p><strong>SCP-5914:</strong> This is kind of disrespectful from you, you know?</p> <div style="clear:both; height: 0px; font-size: 1px"></div> <p><strong>Dr. Rainwards:</strong> You were also-</p> <div style="clear:both; height: 0px; font-size: 1px"></div> <p><strong>SCP-5914:</strong> But fine, however, take this as a warning, I am not taking responsibility if anything goes wrong, got it?</p> <div style="clear:both; height: 0px; font-size: 1px"></div> <p><strong>Dr. Rainwards:</strong> <em>(Silence)</em></p> <div style="clear:both; height: 0px; font-size: 1px"></div> <p><strong>SCP-5914:</strong> Good, now, these &quot;peoples,&quot; &quot;they&quot; are the ones who created the source of all existences, the ones who are more generous than Gods, but their not gods, sort of like one of these, what you humans called as &quot;cosmic entities,&quot; yeah, and these &quot;cosmic entities&quot; are the ones who seek absolute perfection and proper balance within all that comes to existences; they are the <em>[UNDER THE ORDER OF THE O5 COUNCIL, THIS INFORMATION IS REDACTED]</em></p> <div style="clear:both; height: 0px; font-size: 1px"></div> <p><strong>Dr. Rainwards:</strong> What are these <em>[UNDER THE ORDER OF THE O5 COUNCIL, THIS INFORMATION IS REDACTED]</em></p> <div style="clear:both; height: 0px; font-size: 1px"></div> <p><strong>SCP-5914:</strong> They are <em>[UNDER THE ORDER OF THE O5 COUNCIL, THIS INFORMATION IS REDACTED]</em> and it is their job to balance all existences in that &quot;place&quot;. I was one of them. However, I am entirely different from them; I do not care about it. I do not care about the [[REDACTED]] populations.</p> <div style="clear:both; height: 0px; font-size: 1px"></div> <p><strong>Dr. Rainwards:</strong> Okay, but if you will give up and tell me this easily, why did you tell SCP-343 not to say to the Foundation?</p> <div style="clear:both; height: 0px; font-size: 1px"></div> <p><strong>SCP-5914:</strong> As I said, it's my decision. You cannot understand my ways at all; learning how I would be immature, disrespectful, vulgar, and sometimes taking things fucking severe is just a scratch of the surface. You have not to dig deep at all.</p> <div style="clear:both; height: 0px; font-size: 1px"></div> <p><strong>Dr. Rainwards:</strong> All right, is there anything else I need to know?</p> <div style="clear:both; height: 0px; font-size: 1px"></div> <p><strong>SCP-5914:</strong> Fuck no, I cannot tell you; furthermore, this conversation ends here; I'm leaving this shit; I gotta go and play along with &quot;SCP-053&quot; to suppressed this stress. By the way, I am not fucking talking about this again, no matter what you try, conversations like this are fucking not happening again, <em>(SCP-5914 speaks in a low, husky, and sinister voice)</em> <strong>understand?</strong></p> <div style="clear:both; height: 0px; font-size: 1px"></div> <p><em>(SCP-5914 spontaneously disappears.)</em></p> <div style="clear:both; height: 0px; font-size: 1px"></div> <p><strong>&lt;END LOG&gt;</strong></p> <div style="clear:both; height: 0px; font-size: 1px"></div> </blockquote> </div> <p>Researcher Rainwards have reported this to the Foundation; as this was brought to the O5 Council, they have sent out a direct order to all personnel of the Foundation that this information is classified as top-secret. It is to be kept locked away; researcher Rainwards was told to write out a report regarding the information he has collected. He is also advised not to reveal this kind of information that he had heard during the SCP-5914 conversation. As also discussing and decided to do some experimentation on SCP-5914 to learn more about its capabilities.</p> <div class="note"> <p><strong><span style="text-decoration: underline;">Documented-XXXX-07:</span></strong> Rainward's Reports.<br /> On, 02/20/2014 researcher Rainwards have finished his reports about the place that SCP-5914 has explained to him and sent them to the O5 Council.</p> <div style="border:solid 1px #999999; background:#f2f2c2; padding:5px; margin-bottom: 10px;"> <div class="note"> <h4><span>REPORTS TO THE OVERSEER COUNCIL.</span></h4> <h3><span>NOTE: FILE UNDER REVIEW.</span></h3> <p><span style="font-size:150%;"><span style="text-decoration: underline;"><strong>FILE-01</strong></span></span><br /> <strong><span style="text-decoration: underline;">DATE:</span></strong> 11/22/2013</p> <p style="text-align: center;"><strong><span style="font-size:150%;"><tt>EXPERIMENT 1 - TERMINATION OF SCP-682</tt></span></strong></p> <p><strong><span style="text-decoration: underline;">FOREWORD:</span></strong> On 11/13/2013, the Foundation has decided to use SCP-XXXX for the termination process of SCP-682. As they asked SCP-5914 to volunteer, SCP-5914 does not hesitate but just accepts and teleports itself into the observation chamber instantly.<br /> <br /> <br /> <strong><span style="text-decoration: underline;">NAME:</span></strong> Researcher Rainwards with researcher Taylor.<br /> <br /> <br /> <strong><span style="text-decoration: underline;">PROCEDURES:</span></strong> The SCP-5914 forms out a pistol gun in its hand. At the same time, SCP-682 growls and moves to the back corner, SCP-5914 points the pistol gun and fires with an unseen speed, SCP-682 was shot on the head, the reptilian's body temperature starts to increase fast before exploding into pieces and gets disintegrated, termination of SCP-682 was a success. However, SCP-5914 regenerates SCP-682 back to normal and walks out of the observation chamber.<br /> <br /> <br /> <strong><span style="text-decoration: underline;">AFTERWORD:</span></strong> When SCP-5914 walks out of the observation chamber, the researchers asked why it brought SCP-682 back to life. SCP-5914 responded that SCP-682 was one of its favorite SCPs in the Foundation, although it's true that SCP-682 is evil, however, its very cool to SCP-5914, so successfully terminating it would cause SCP-5914 to feel very dull.<br /> <br /> <br /> <strong><span style="text-decoration: underline;">RESULTS:</span></strong> <span style="text-decoration: line-through;">The termination of SCP-682 was a success as 100% of its body was destroyed, leaving no trace</span> The termination of SCP-682 wasn't a success as after it was a success, SCP-5914 has brought it back to life.</p> </div> <div class="note"> <p><span style="font-size:150%;"><span style="text-decoration: underline;"><strong>FILE-02</strong></span></span><br /> <strong><span style="text-decoration: underline;">DATE:</span></strong> 12/01/2013</p> <p style="text-align: center;"><strong><span style="font-size:150%;"><tt>EXPERIMENT 2 - ANOMALOUS ABILITY-01</tt></span></strong></p> <p><strong><span style="text-decoration: underline;">FOREWORD:</span></strong> On 12/01/2013, SCP-5914 was asked by the Foundation to demonstrate one of its anomalous abilities. SCP-5914 that time was in the middle of watching &quot;The Amazing World of Gumball&quot; with SCP-053 to tell the facility guards to screw off. Later on, while walking back to its containment cell, SCP-5914 stopped by the observation chamber and gathered the researchers who were volunteering to launch experimentation upon the anomaly, and decided to experiment because today is one of its day-off work in a very disrespectful attitude.<br /> <br /> <br /> <strong><span style="text-decoration: underline;">NAME:</span></strong> Researcher Rainwards with researcher Taylor.<br /> <br /> <br /> <strong><span style="text-decoration: underline;">PROCEDURES:</span></strong> SCP-5914 raised out its right hand and did a finger snap. The surroundings of the researchers begin to shatter into millions of pieces and reform back to normal.<br /> <br /> <br /> <strong><span style="text-decoration: underline;">AFTERWORD:</span></strong> SCP-5914 decides to walk off to SCP-5031 containment unit to taste one of its cooking foods, at the same time showing it some professional chefs from different universes.<br /> <br /> <br /> <strong><span style="text-decoration: underline;">RESULTS:</span></strong> SCP-5914's reality-altering effects seemingly shattered the surroundings of everything and breaks reality like it is nothing but just a fragile-looking glass. The anomaly wasn't lying when it said it could break reality anytime it wants to.</p> </div> <div class="note"> <p><span style="font-size:150%;"><span style="text-decoration: underline;"><strong>FILE-03</strong></span></span><br /> <strong><span style="text-decoration: underline;">DATE:</span></strong> 12/15/2013</p> <p style="text-align: center;"><strong><span style="font-size:150%;"><tt>EXPERIMENT 3 - ANOMALOUS ABILITY-02</tt></span></strong></p> <p><strong><span style="text-decoration: underline;">FOREWORD:</span></strong> On 12/15/2013, ever since the previous experiment, SCP-XXXX denies rapidly not volunteering in other experiments for the whole week. Until this date, SCP-5914 was asked to manifest some life-forms, any life-forms that it wants to, SCP-5914 at this moment just accepted it after making a mess by painting insulting words on the whole cafeteria of Site-19.<br /> <br /> <br /> <strong><span style="text-decoration: underline;">NAME:</span></strong> Researcher Rainwards with researcher Taylor.<br /> <br /> <br /> <strong><span style="text-decoration: underline;">PROCEDURES:</span></strong> SCP-5914 increased the observation chamber's size. It manifested up to a hundred and fifty butt naked farting human life-forms inside the observation chamber. It is also shown to laugh non-stop at the farting subjects that were manifested into a reality.<br /> <br /> <br /> <strong><span style="text-decoration: underline;">AFTERWORD:</span></strong> SCP-5914 walks out of the room while laughing non-stop as it said to stop by to SCP-053 to show the little girl some new cartoon shows and explains to her about those.<br /> <br /> <br /> <strong><span style="text-decoration: underline;">RESULTS:</span></strong> SCP-5914 can manifest a large amount of any life-forms it desires, regardless of whether those life-forms are stupid or imperfect through views of surroundings. It also seems to find it very funny.</p> </div> <div class="note"> <p><span style="font-size:150%;"><span style="text-decoration: underline;"><strong>FILE-04</strong></span></span><br /> <strong><span style="text-decoration: underline;">DATE:</span></strong> 12/15/2013</p> <p style="text-align: center;"><strong><span style="font-size:150%;"><tt>EXPERIMENT 4 - ANOMALOUS ABILITY-03</tt></span></strong></p> <p><strong><span style="text-decoration: underline;">FOREWORD:</span></strong> On 12/15/2013, ever since the previous experiment, SCP-5914 denies rapidly not volunteering in other experiments for the whole week. Until this date, SCP-5914 was asked to manifest some life-forms, any life-forms that it wants to, SCP-5914 at this moment just accepted it after making a mess by painting insulting words on the whole cafeteria of Site-19.<br /> <br /> <br /> <strong><span style="text-decoration: underline;">NAME:</span></strong> Researcher Rainwards with researcher Taylor.<br /> <br /> <br /> <strong><span style="text-decoration: underline;">PROCEDURES:</span></strong> SCP-5914 increased the observation chamber's size. It manifested up to a hundred and fifty butt naked farting human life-forms inside the observation chamber. It is also shown to laugh non-stop at the farting subjects that were manifested into a reality.<br /> <br /> <br /> <strong><span style="text-decoration: underline;">AFTERWORD:</span></strong> SCP-5914 walks out of the room while de-manifesting its creations while laughing non-stop as it said to stop by to SCP-053 to show the little girl some new cartoon shows and explains to her.<br /> <br /> <br /> <strong><span style="text-decoration: underline;">RESULTS:</span></strong> SCP-5914 can manifest a large amount of any life-forms it desires, regardless of whether those life-forms are stupid or imperfect through views of surroundings. It also seems to find it very funny.</p> </div> <div class="note"> <p><span style="font-size:150%;"><span style="text-decoration: underline;"><strong>FILE-05</strong></span></span><br /> <strong><span style="text-decoration: underline;">DATE:</span></strong> 12/16/2013</p> <p style="text-align: center;"><strong><span style="font-size:150%;"><tt>EXPERIMENT 5 - ANOMALOUS ABILITY-04</tt></span></strong></p> <p><strong><span style="text-decoration: underline;">FOREWORD:</span></strong> On 12/16/2013, SCP-5914 was asked to gather a group of Class-D subjects into SCP-5914-01 and let them react to some things it wants them to know. SCP-5914 proceeded to do so.<br /> <br /> <br /> <strong><span style="text-decoration: underline;">NAME:</span></strong> Researcher Rainwards with researcher Taylor.<br /> <br /> <br /> <strong><span style="text-decoration: underline;">PROCEDURES:</span></strong> SCP-5914 gathered all of them into SCP-5914-01 inside of the observation chamber as it first explains to them how &quot;fun&quot; it is to be a Class-D. SCP-5914 shows them an alternate universe called <em>&quot;SCP - Containment Breach&quot;</em> where the story is based on D-Class personnel designated as &quot;D-9341&quot; who was brought to clean up the containment chamber of SCP-173. Fortunately, the facility has an incident related to a power outage, resulting in a big containment breach event.<br /> <br /> <br /> <strong><span style="text-decoration: underline;">AFTERWORD:</span></strong> The D-Class personnel finds it exciting and fun. However, when the researchers have asked SCP-5914 what reality has shown to the D-Class subjects, SCP-5914 explains that it is not a reality but gameplay developed in a universe where the SCP-Foundation is known to all but does not exist due to being a fictional organization.<br /> <br /> <br /> <strong><span style="text-decoration: underline;">RESULTS:</span></strong> SCP-5914 was able to impress the D-Class subjects; however, the universe it showed was just gameplay, assuming that the anomaly is either playing a prank/trick or just trying to give positive inspiration for the D-Class subjects.</p> </div> <div class="note"> <p><span style="font-size:150%;"><span style="text-decoration: underline;"><strong>FILE-06</strong></span></span><br /> <strong><span style="text-decoration: underline;">DATE:</span></strong> 01/13/2013</p> <p style="text-align: center;"><strong><span style="font-size:150%;"><tt>EXPERIMENT 6 &#8212; INTELLIGENCE LEVEL TESTING-01</tt></span></strong></p> <p><strong><span style="text-decoration: underline;">FOREWORD:</span></strong> On 01/13/2014, SCP-5914 was asked to test its intelligence level upon doing an examination test that the Foundation has made for it. SCP-5914 has 10 minutes to read through the given documents and later on has 30 minutes written down answers without using any of its anomalous abilities.<br /> <br /> <br /> <strong><span style="text-decoration: underline;">NAME:</span></strong> Researcher Rainwards with researcher Taylor.<br /> <br /> <br /> <strong><span style="text-decoration: underline;">PROCEDURES:</span></strong> SCP-5914 leaks through the documents for only 3 minutes before proceeding to the examination test immediately due to it wanting to bring SCP-053 to meet SCP-999, it writes down all the answers. It finishes the test for only 15 minutes without re-checking to see if there are any errors. Later on, after another 15 minutes have passed, the Foundation's researchers checked on the exam and saw that it has no errors.<br /> <br /> <br /> <strong><span style="text-decoration: underline;">AFTERWORD:</span></strong> SCP-5914 walks out of the observation chamber after swearing for a few times as it has taken SCP-053 to SCP-999 in the aftermath.<br /> <br /> <br /> <strong><span style="text-decoration: underline;">RESULTS:</span></strong> SCP-5914 could score a direct 100/100 with no much effort. It looks like the subject has a great photographic memory.</p> </div> <div class="note"> <p><span style="font-size:150%;"><span style="text-decoration: underline;"><strong>FILE-07</strong></span></span><br /> <strong><span style="text-decoration: underline;">DATE:</span></strong> 01/20/2013</p> <p style="text-align: center;"><strong><span style="font-size:150%;"><tt>EXPERIMENT 7 &#8212; INTELLIGENCE LEVEL TESTING-02</tt></span></strong></p> <p><strong><span style="text-decoration: underline;">FOREWORD:</span></strong> On 01/20/2014, SCP-5914 was asked to demonstrate its knowledge in knowing what are the containment procedures of SCP-096 and SCP-2371 without taking a peek through.<br /> <br /> <br /> <strong><span style="text-decoration: underline;">NAME:</span></strong> Researcher Rainwards with researcher Taylor.<br /> <br /> <br /> <strong><span style="text-decoration: underline;">PROCEDURES:</span></strong> SCP-5914 responded that the containment procedures of SCP-096 are to be kept in a 5&#160;m x 5&#160;m x 5&#160;m airtight steel cube at all times. Weekly checks for any cracks or holes are mandatory. There are to be absolutely no video surveillance or visual tools of any kind inside SCP-096's cell. Security personnel will use pre-installed pressure sensors and laser detectors to ensure SCP-096's presence inside the cell. SCP-2317 is to be secured at Containment Area-179 in a reinforced 3m x 3m x 3m containment chamber. Armed guards are to be in place at all times to prevent unauthorized access to the facility.<br /> <br /> <br /> <strong><span style="text-decoration: underline;">AFTERWORD:</span></strong> Researchers have asked how calm SCP-5914 was able to know. SCP-5914 responded that it had sawed the description of the containment procedures thousands of times, and it felt extremely bored after having to sit and let the gathered individuals inside of SCP-5914-01 watch it. SCP-5914 soon walks out of the observation chamber as it stops by the containment chamber of SCP-5031 to taste its food along with SCP-053 and SCP-999, giving it some cooking books, and shows its more cooking lessons on the widescreen.<br /> <br /> <br /> <strong><span style="text-decoration: underline;">RESULTS:</span></strong> SCP-5914 explained the containment procedures of SCP-096 and SCP-2317 with no wrong information.</p> </div> <div class="note"> <p><span style="font-size:150%;"><span style="text-decoration: underline;"><strong>FILE-08</strong></span></span><br /> <strong><span style="text-decoration: underline;">DATE:</span></strong> 01/25/2014</p> <p style="text-align: center;"><strong><span style="font-size:150%;"><tt>EXPERIMENT 8 &#8212; ANOMALOUS ABILITIES-05</tt></span></strong></p> <p><strong><span style="text-decoration: underline;">FOREWORD:</span></strong> On 01/25/2014, SCP-5914 was asked to see whether it can transport the researchers to the &quot;The Barrelplex&quot;. However, SCP-5914 immediately shouts out that it doesn't want to, for the peoples there fear it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <strong><span style="text-decoration: underline;">NAME:</span></strong> Researcher Rainwards with researcher Taylor.<br /> <br /> <br /> <strong><span style="text-decoration: underline;">PROCEDURES:</span></strong> The researchers did not argue and asked for another request. If it can transport a group of Class-D subjects to a parallel universe, SCP-5914, without hesitation, transports the Class-D subjects into another reality while sitting on a levitating bean bag. After about five days have passed, SCP-5914 was once again called to the observation chamber, where it was instructed to transport the Class-D crew back to the observation chamber. SCP-5914 said that there is only one alive D-Class subject left. The rest have died. The subject also explains how did they die. However, later on, transported the last D-Class subject back, the D-Class, subject D-458103 was crawling in fear, researchers have asked what did the subject saw, the subject exclaimed that what they say are the things that no one must ever saw, it is unknown whether what reality did SCP-5914 transport them into.<br /> <br /> <br /> <strong><span style="text-decoration: underline;">AFTERWORD:</span></strong> SCP-5914 walks out of the observation chamber; the researchers have asked SCP-5914 why did it begin to volunteer in experiments like this. SCP-5914 revealed that it has powerful precognition in seeing what will happen next. It also exclaimed that the Foundation would only do nine experiments on it, tomorrow is the last one, so it won't hesitate but to volunteer in the last two ones. It then exited the observation chamber, went back to its containment cell, and watched one of its favorite universes.<br /> <br /> <br /> <strong><span style="text-decoration: underline;">RESULTS:</span></strong> It is unknown what reality the Class-D subjects saw. They did not provide any information about that place other than this &quot;The End of the World.&quot; It also reveals a new piece of information that SCP-5914 has a powerful vision of knowing what'll happen next. However, SCP-5914 seems to have revealed something else. It claimed that the beings that existed in the &quot;Barrelplex&quot; feared it. This is getting weird, firstly. In the interview with researcher Rainwards, SCP-5914 claims that it was seen as mistaken and was banished. However, now it said that beings there feared it, what does this suppose to mean?</p> </div> <div class="note"> <p><span style="font-size:150%;"><span style="text-decoration: underline;"><strong>FILE-09</strong></span></span><br /> <strong><span style="text-decoration: underline;">DATE:</span></strong> 02/04/2014</p> <p style="text-align: center;"><strong><span style="font-size:150%;"><tt>EXPERIMENT 9 &#8212; ANOMALOUS ABILITIES-06</tt></span></strong></p> <p><strong><span style="text-decoration: underline;">FOREWORD:</span></strong> On 02/04/2014, it was also the final experiment that'll be launch on SCP-5914 as that was what it had claimed yesterday. SCP-5914 was asked to see whether if it can resurrect one of the neutralized SCPs.<br /> <br /> <strong><span style="text-decoration: underline;">PROCEDURES:</span></strong> SCP-5914 did not hesitate but immediately raises its hands and forms a plain cardboard box that is 32&#160;cm x 20&#160;cm x 26&#160;cm. It is spray-painted silver on the interior and exterior, and the words &quot;HERE BE DRAGONS&quot; are handwritten in black permanent marker on the lid of the container. It was SCP-1762, and all of its instances were also fully restored with no errors along the way. However, the box disappears all of a sudden.<br /> <br /> <br /> <strong><span style="text-decoration: underline;">NAME:</span></strong> Researcher Rainwards with researcher Taylor.<br /> <br /> <br /> <strong><span style="text-decoration: underline;">AFTERWORD:</span></strong> SCP-5914 walks out of the observation chamber; the researchers were about to asked SCP-XXXX why the box disappears. SCP-5914 responded, &quot;Isn't it obvious fuckers, have you ever heard, what comes up, must come down? That's the rules of death and life&quot; it then exits the observation room.<br /> <br /> <br /> <strong><span style="text-decoration: underline;">RESULTS:</span></strong> It would appear like SCP-5914 can resurrect neutralized SCPs without much effort. As it also &quot;understands&quot; the rules between life and death.</p> </div> <p><span style="font-size:150%;"><span style="text-decoration: underline;"><strong>FILE-010</strong></span></span><br /> <strong><span style="text-decoration: underline;">DATE:</span></strong> 02/05/2014</p> <p style="text-align: center;"><strong><span style="font-size:150%;"><tt>DOCUMENT 10 &#8212; THE &quot;BARRELPLEX&quot;</tt></span></strong></p> </div> </div> <br /> <tt>&gt; ERROR OCCUR&#8230;</tt> <p><tt>&gt; UNABLE TO ACCESS FILE.</tt></p> <p><tt>&gt; FILE DELETED BY @#@#*$$</tt></p> <p><tt>&gt; VIRUS DETECTED&#8230;</tt></p> <p><tt>&gt; RESTARTING CLIENT&#8230;</tt></p> <p><tt>&gt; LOGGING OFF IN 3 SECONDS&#8230;</tt></p> <p><tt>&gt; LOG OUT SUCCESS.</tt></p> <p><tt>&gt; SHUTTING DOWN IN 5 SECONDS&#8230;</tt></p> <p><tt>&gt; SHUTTING DOWN&#8230;</tt></p> <div class="footnotes-footer"> <div class="title">Footnotes</div> <div class="footnote-footer" id="footnote-773238-1"><a href="javascript:;" >1</a>. Currently, the entity is exceptionally stubborn and not obeying the Foundation's instructions/commands. The anomaly has kept on breaching the containment chamber while causing out containment breaches most of the time for its enjoyments, so it's not yet contained. Instead, it sees the Foundation as a place to explore freely and do whatever it wants to.</div> <div class="footnote-footer" id="footnote-773238-2"><a href="javascript:;" >2</a>. However. Now, it has no intention of doing so</div> <div class="footnote-footer" id="footnote-773238-3"><a href="javascript:;" >3</a>. It means no proper physical form. Though they may have physical avatars or bodies, their true essence exists non-physically, whether as a soul, as energy, or as an abstract concept. However, in SCP-5914 cases, it is considered differently. The entity can shapeshift or sometimes manifest its non-physical avatar and turns it into a physical avatar.</div> <div class="footnote-footer" id="footnote-773238-4"><a href="javascript:;" >4</a>. The forms it has manifested into/taken can either be from an individual that it has once encounter or an individual that does not exist. However, the entity took men/boys' appearance while doing its &quot;job,&quot; presuming that it is a male.</div> <div class="footnote-footer" id="footnote-773238-5"><a href="javascript:;" >5</a>. This is not its proper form.</div> <div class="footnote-footer" id="footnote-773238-6"><a href="javascript:;" >6</a>. Currently, it is unknown whether what does the &quot;Barrelplex&quot; looks like.</div> <div class="footnote-footer" id="footnote-773238-7"><a href="javascript:;" >7</a>. In-short, it has absolute control over everything irrespective of whether if it's space and time, reality, laws of physics, nature, and events. The anomaly would also be able to control everything even when it is outside of SCP-5914-01. SCP-5914-01 is just a place to hide the gathered individuals to let them spectate in other universes to avoid getting caught, disrupting, or getting disrupted by the individuals seen on the widescreen.</div> <div class="footnote-footer" id="footnote-773238-8"><a href="javascript:;" >8</a>. In short parallel universes.</div> <div class="footnote-footer" id="footnote-773238-9"><a href="javascript:;" >9</a>. However, it depends on the entity's decision; it would sometimes let the gathered individuals figure it out themselves.</div> <div class="footnote-footer" id="footnote-773238-10"><a href="javascript:;" >10</a>. While being distracted by another, spacing out for a moment, thinking/imagining other things&#8230;</div> <div class="footnote-footer" id="footnote-773238-11"><a href="javascript:;" >11</a>. Which are its free time/day off of work</div> <div class="footnote-footer" id="footnote-773238-12"><a href="javascript:;" >12</a>. Even if it is forbidden to, it would just go out of its containment cell anytime it wants without the Foundation's permission. It also means the entity is sometimes very stubborn and would be considered as a scapegoat.</div> <div class="footnote-footer" id="footnote-773238-13"><a href="javascript:;" >13</a>. Sometimes from the universe that it is currently living in, which the Foundation always has to keep a very close look upon the gathered individuals to, later on, wipe out their memories after SCP-5914 finishes its job.</div> </div> <p>by <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/godlyuser" ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=6876114&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1607979346" alt="GodlyUser" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=6876114)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/godlyuser" >GodlyUser</a></span></p> 
