				<title>The Chorus</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-5934</link>
				<description>

&lt;div style=&quot;text-align: right;&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Item #:&lt;/strong&gt; SCP-5934&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Object Class:&lt;/strong&gt; safe&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Special Containment Procedures:&lt;/strong&gt; Subject should be allowed to roam the facility between 6&amp;#160;A.M and 7 P.M, and should be placed in a 3x3x3 meter containment area for sleeping. if another Scp breaches containment, The subject should be moved to the loose Scp if it is Euclid or above.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Description:&lt;/strong&gt; Scp 5934 is a group of glowing orbs that can change their colouration at will. If any sentient entities enter within a 5 Meter radius, Scp 5934 will begin to sing. this song has a soothing effect on all exposed sentient entities. It is unknown why the subject&#039;s song has this effect, further research is required. Scp 5934 can be used to contain Scps and suppress D-class personnel.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Addendum:&lt;/strong&gt; Scp 5934 seems to dislike certain entities, and will sing a song that will enrage the target. there is no obvious connection between the disliked entities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A list of Disliked entities&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Scp 096&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Scp 106&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Scp 173&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Scp 303&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;D-238&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;D-566&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;D-926&lt;/p&gt;
